.TH SPACEGL_SERVER 1 "2026-04-19" "SpaceGL @VERSION@" "SpaceGL Manual"
.SH NAME
spacegl_server \- SpaceGL galaxy server daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B spacegl_server
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B spacegl_server
is the central game server for the SpaceGL multi-user 3D space engine.
It manages galaxy state, player sessions, NPC entities, and secure
communication channels via shared memory (SHM) and TCP networking on
port 5000.
.PP
Server and decks share a deployment master key, read from
.BR SPACEGL_KEY_FILE ,
then
.BR SPACEGL_KEY ,
then
.I ~/.spacegl/key
(created when none exists); the launcher script
.BR spacegl-server (1)
asks for it interactively when
.B SPACEGL_KEY
is not set.
.PP
Each server also has an identity of its own, an Ed25519 key created on
the first boot in
.IR [DATA\-DIR]/server_identity.key .
It signs every handshake (wire revision 4) and the decks pin it; its
fingerprint is printed at boot and by
.BR \-\-print\-identity .
.PP
Every connection on port 5000 runs inside TLS 1.3 (wire revision 5); there
is no plaintext mode. The certificate is made at start-up, in memory, from
the identity key: there is no certificate file to install or renew. A deck
older than revision 5 (its hello in clear) is refused at the first byte,
and a connection that does not complete its TLS handshake within 10 s is
closed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-d
Enable debug mode (verbose logging).
.TP
.B \-\-data-dir DIR
Root directory for the server's persistent state: the
.IR captains/ \(em captain profiles, identity records and frequency
keys \(em and the
.I galaxy.dat
file are stored under this directory instead of the current working
directory (the default, kept for backward compatibility). The directory
is created at startup if it does not exist. Note: pointing the server at
a directory without an existing
galaxy.dat
starts a fresh galaxy.
.TP
.B \-\-io=MODE
Event-loop I/O strategy.
.BR legacy (default):
the original blocking per-packet read path (read_all() bounded by a
5 s poll): a client that stalls mid-packet can hold the single-threaded
loop, and with it every other player, for up to 5 seconds.
.BR async :
the professional non-blocking architecture: accepted client sockets are
explicitly non-blocking (O_NONBLOCK), the request handler never waits
on a socket, and a recv() returning EAGAIN mid-packet stages the
partial packet in the per-connection RX buffer (HEADER/BODY/TEXT state
machine) and returns to the epoll loop; on the next EPOLLIN it resumes
from the saved cursor and processes the packet only when complete.
Small replies are staged and drained on EPOLLOUT, so the loop never
blocks on send either: a stalled client can at most occupy its own
session.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-identity
Print the server identity (its fingerprint, then the 64 hex digits of its
Ed25519 public key) and exit; the identity is created if it does not exist
yet; no master key is needed. The decks pin this key: compare the
fingerprint they show on the first connection with it, or give the key
to them in
.BR SPACEGL_SERVER_KEY .
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display usage information and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SPACEGL_KEY_FILE
Path of a file holding the master key (64 hex digits, mode 0600: the
server refuses a file readable by others). Preferred over
.BR SPACEGL_KEY .
.TP
.B SPACEGL_KEY
The master key as a string (legacy; fallback
.IR ~/.spacegl/key ).
.TP
.B SPACEGL_TICK_THREADS
OpenMP threads of the 60 Hz tick's parallel loops, 1 to 64 (default 1).
The loops are short: on most machines a second thread saves nothing and
doubles the CPU time (it spins at every join), and a thread the system
takes away from its CPU holds the whole tick for a time slice.
.SH PERFORMANCE
The game thread times every tick: the logic, the wait for the game lock,
the galaxy save image, the network updates, the telemetry, how late it
woke up and the CPU time it used. When ticks exceed the 16.7 ms budget it
logs, at most every 10 seconds, one WARNING (category PERFORMANCE) with
their number and the worst one broken down by phase; a tick whose CPU time
is under half its duration is reported as waiting for a CPU (the machine
is busy, not the server). At shutdown it logs the totals ("game loop:
N ticks, K over the 16.7 ms budget ..."). Selected with
.BR \-\-log\-category=PERFORMANCE .
.SH SYSTEM SERVICE
Optional. The installation provides the systemd unit
.BR spacegl-server.service ,
which is never enabled by itself: running the server by hand keeps
working. To use it, put the master key (64 hex digits, the same the decks
use) in
.I /etc/spacegl/key
(mode 0600, root only) and run
.BR "systemctl enable \-\-now spacegl-server" .
The service runs as a transient unprivileged user in a sandbox, receives
the key as a systemd credential
.RB ( SPACEGL_KEY_FILE
points into the credentials directory), keeps its data directory in
.I /var/lib/spacegl
and logs to the journal
.RB ( "journalctl \-u spacegl-server" ;
its identity: add
.BR "\-g \(dqServer identity\(dq" ).
SIGTERM from
.B systemctl stop
saves the galaxy before the server exits; it is restarted after a crash.
Extra options go in
.I /etc/spacegl/server.env
as
.BR SPACEGL_SERVER_OPTS="\-\-io=async" ;
local changes to the unit with
.BR "systemctl edit spacegl-server" .
Do not start a second server by hand while the service runs: both need
port 5000.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/bin/spacegl_server
Server executable.
.TP
.I [DATA\-DIR]/galaxy.dat
Serialized galaxy state (default: ./galaxy.dat).
.TP
.I [DATA\-DIR]/captains/
captain profiles, identity records and frequency keys
(default: ./captains/).
.TP
.I [DATA\-DIR]/server_identity.key
The server's Ed25519 identity (private key, 64 hex digits, mode 0600),
created on the first boot; it signs every handshake (wire revision 4).
Back it up with the data directory: a new key looks like another server
to every deck that has met this one.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/spacegl-server.service
The optional system service (see SYSTEM SERVICE).
.TP
.I /etc/spacegl/key
The master key of the service (mode 0600, root only).
.TP
.I /etc/spacegl/server.env
Optional settings of the service
.RB ( SPACEGL_SERVER_OPTS ,
.BR SPACEGL_LOG_LEVEL ).
.TP
.I /var/lib/spacegl/
The data directory of the service.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR spacegl_client (1),
.BR spacegl-server (1),
.BR spacegl_3dview (1),
.BR spacegl_vulkan (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
